    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "wilkins_2013_bragg_centennial",
        "page": 2,
        "quote": "while Lawrence was walking along the Backs in Cambridge one day in the late autumn of 1912, in a flash of insight he conceived of the relatively simple explanation that the diffraction patterns from zinc blende observed by Laue and colleagues could be ascribed to the reflection of electromagnetic waves of short wavelength from planes of atoms in the crystal."
